  },
  "body": "The `<xmp>` element was removed from the \"special\" elements list, apparently inadvertently, in 77c3dc4863a212cc944eede0e09907bec52cde43..\n\n`<xmp>` is still handled specially in the \"in body\" insertion mode, in the fragment serialization algorithm, and in the HTML fragment parsing algorithm.  Further, because it was (previously) a member of the \"special\" set, it was handled differently by the adoption agency algorithm and by the \"in body\" insertion mode rules for `<li>`, `<dd>` and `<dt>` start tags and \"any other end tag\".\n",
